Z||000000||ccollins||01-26-2001||10:44 AM||||What do you think a P/W, P/Locks, P/Mirror electrical unit with all the swithces in working order will cost? <P>Anyone have one for sale? <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||01-26-2001||11:05 AM||||Well, there isn't "a unit".  p/w, p/m, and p/l are all separate options.  They each have their own necessary assemblies (motors, switches, wiring harness, relays, etc.)  The easiest thing is to find a donor car that has all these options, in working order, and transplant the parts to your car.<P>I bought a set of doors with all these options, along with all the associated wiring, switches, relays, etc. -- in addition to an aero front fascia, sunroof, dash, entire center console unit and many additional smaller parts for $400.  It was a good deal!!<P>You can also buy these options aftermarket but I'm not sure from whom or for how much.<P>Check the article in Ogre's Cave (see link at bottom of page) for what is involved in adding power windows to your car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ccollins||01-26-2001||11:14 AM||||I'm talking about the just the unit that sits on the center console that has all the push buttons.   Not adding all these options to a car that doesn't have them.  <P>All motors and switches are currently working. Mine is all scratched up and I would like to replace it. <BR>||||reg||1
